' 55 Trust boundaries of Reified RSpaces: the untrusted inputs, the parts of
' the node that check them, and the controls SC-1 to SC-22 of security.md.
'
' Source of the figure of ../security.md (section 3). The figure restates the
' control table of that document. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the left to the right:
'   1. Four kinds of untrusted input reach the node: the program of a deploy,
'      the code of a user agent, the blocks and pages of a peer, and the
'      answers of an external service.
'   2. The program passes the normalizer and the reducer hooks, then the
'      system processes and the space agents, and last the substrate.
'   3. The code of a user agent runs as an ordinary program. It reaches a
'      space only through the capabilities that the node built.
'   4. The blocks of a peer pass native replay and the merger, and its LFS
'      pages pass the validation of the importer.
'   5. The answers of a service are advisory or recorded, and the exact
'      engine decides.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 55-security-trust-boundaries.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 55-security-trust-boundaries
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam PackageBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ComponentBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
left to right direction
title Trust boundaries of Reified RSpaces and their controls

package "Untrusted inputs" as INPUTS $rrs_reject {
  component PROGRAM $rrs_reject [
  **Program of a deploy**
  arbitrary Rholang of a deploy author
  ]
  component AGENTCODE $rrs_reject [
  **Code of a user agent**
  the Rholang of an agent author
  ]
  component PEER $rrs_reject [
  **Peer node**
  blocks, journals, LFS pages
  ]
  component SERVICE $rrs_reject [
  **External service**
  ChromaDB answers, embeddings
  ]
}

package "Node: program boundary" as NODE $rrs_host {
  component NORMALIZER $rrs_syntax [
  **Normalizer and decoders**
  fields of a construct: exactly the
  canonical image (SC-1)
  ]
  component HOOKS $rrs_host [
  **Reducer hooks**
  routing and space references (SC-2, SC-3)
  persistent calls and params (SC-5, SC-6)
  seq rules, dangling ids, joins (SC-10 to SC-12)
  ]
  component PROCESSES $rrs_system [
  **System processes**
  factory gates (SC-7), bare handle (SC-4)
  reply names (SC-8), internal ops (SC-15, SC-16)
  ]
  component AGENTS $rrs_agent [
  **Space agents**
  theories fail closed (SC-9)
  bounds of each operation (SC-13)
  deterministic choices (SC-18)
  ]
  database SUBSTRATE $rrs_substrate [
  **Substrate**
  prefix-atomic commit and
  deploy revert (SC-14)
  ]
}

package "Consensus boundary" as CONSENSUS $rrs_substrate {
  component REPLAY $rrs_substrate [
  **Native replay**
  fails closed on a forged row (SC-19)
  ]
  component MERGER $rrs_substrate [
  **Merger**
  counter races and event coverage (SC-20)
  ]
  component IMPORTER $rrs_substrate [
  **LFS importer**
  validates each page (SC-21)
  ]
}

package "Agent boundary" as AGENTB $rrs_object {
  component CAPS $rrs_name [
  **Capabilities of a translation**
  matchers, bodies and the sink:
  built by the node, decoded strictly (SC-15)
  no persistent send (SC-16)
  ]
  component OBLIGATIONS $rrs_object [
  **Obligations ASO-1 to ASO-3**
  not checked by the node,
  checked by the conformance kit (SC-17)
  ]
}

component MIRROR $rrs_service [
**Service boundary**
advisory ids and recorded outputs;
the exact engine decides (SC-22)
]

PROGRAM -[$rrs_flow]-> NORMALIZER : source text
NORMALIZER -[$rrs_flow]-> HOOKS : normalized Par
HOOKS -[$rrs_flow]-> PROCESSES : calls on op channels and handles
PROCESSES -[$rrs_flow]-> AGENTS : space jobs
HOOKS -[$rrs_flow]-> AGENTS : routed sends and receives
AGENTS -[$rrs_effect]-> SUBSTRATE : staged operations, one commit
AGENTCODE -[$rrs_flow]-> CAPS : calls on the capabilities
CAPS -[$rrs_flow]-> PROCESSES : matcher op, sink, handle consume
AGENTCODE -[$rrs_relation]-> OBLIGATIONS : author keeps
PEER -[$rrs_flow]-> REPLAY : blocks and journals
PEER -[$rrs_flow]-> MERGER : sibling blocks
PEER -[$rrs_flow]-> IMPORTER : LFS pages
SERVICE -[$rrs_flow]-> MIRROR : answers
MIRROR -[$rrs_relation]-> AGENTS : ids as hints only
REPLAY -[$rrs_relation]-> SUBSTRATE : the same operations as play
IMPORTER -[$rrs_effect]-> SUBSTRATE : state of a root

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_reject>     | untrusted input |
|<$rrs_host>       | node at the baseline: the reducer |
|<$rrs_syntax>     | syntax layer |
|<$rrs_system>     | system processes |
|<$rrs_agent>      | space agents and user agents |
|<$rrs_name>       | capabilities |
|<$rrs_substrate>  | substrate and consensus parts |
|<$rrs_service>    | external services |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_flow>       | input or call |
|<$rrs_effect>     | effect on the stored state |
|<$rrs_relation>   | check or rule |
endlegend
@enduml
